TextField input = new TextField();
Label echo = new Label();
input.textProperty().addListener((obs, oldVal, newVal) -> {
echo.setText("typed: " + newVal);
});

// echo always equals input.text reversed
echo.textProperty().bind(
Bindings.createStringBinding(
() -> new StringBuilder(input.getText()).reverse().toString(),
input.textProperty()
)
);
// expression bindings
DoubleProperty a = new SimpleDoubleProperty(2);
DoubleProperty b = new SimpleDoubleProperty(3);
DoubleBinding sum = a.add(b); // sum updates when a or b changes
sum.addListener((o, ov, nv) -> System.out.println("sum = " + nv));
a.set(10); // prints sum = 13
Bindings keep UI state in sync with model state without manual wiring.

All scene-graph changes must happen on the JavaFX Application Thread. From a background thread, use:
Platform.runLater(() -> label.setText("done"));
For longer work, use a Task<T> which runs call() on a background thread and exposes succeeded/failed callbacks on the JavaFX thread.

